lucy_sales: Quick sync Eva at MeridianEdge wants a 90-day pilot. Requirements: websocket streaming, function/tool calls that return strictly validated JSON per tenant, SAML SSO, and customer KMS. Also asked for a Rust SDK sample they can drop into their service, a one-pager runbook for ephemeral tokens and reconnect, plus a pricing ballpark for ~5M tokens/day (peaks ~50 rps). Any hard blockers?
eva_cust: Wed like minimal ops overhead; prefer short-lived creds and an example of how to surface schema validation failures to our logs/alerts.
omar_se: Plan: hosted demo to move fast; Dedicated if they need isolation/SLA. For Rust SDK Ill prepare a tiny example showing streaming + handling function_call events + validating against JSON Schema. I'll include a small test harness too.
omar_se: POC checklist: 1) JSON schemas for each function; 2) SAML IdP metadata; 3) KMS intent (BYOK vs Redwood-managed); 4) latency target (p95); 5) residency constraints.
taku_prod: Security quick answers to include in the sales pack: TLS1.3, AES-256 at rest, BYOK supported for Private/Dedicated, configurable audit logs, SOC2 summary available. I'll attach a short FAQ link.
sec_bot: Security questionnaire uploaded: https://redwood.internal/sq/meridianedge-1755554321 (sales+sec) :lock:
ivan_infra: Handshake & runbook highlights: use ephemeral tokens TTL~1h, rotate by reconnect (request new token at T-15m), avoid in-stream swaps. Backpressure: client smoothing + server continuous batching. Provide curl/wscat and a tiny reconnect state-machine example.
omar_se: Rust SDK sketch (send-only view):```rust
let client = RedClient::new(api_key);
let mut stream = client.stream("redwood-chat-1");
stream.send(json!({"input":"Get orders tenant=21","functions":[{"name":"fetch_orders","schema":{/*...*/}}]}));
for evt in stream.recv() {
  match evt.kind.as_str() {
    "function_call" => { let res = call_local_service(&evt.args); stream.send(json!({"function_response":res})); }
    "chunk" => print!("{}", evt.text),
    "validation_error" => log::error!("schema failed: {:?}", evt.errors),
    _ => {}
  }
}
```
ivan_infra: Pricing note: propose (A) Hosted pilot blended cap for 90d with convert-to-commit option; (B) Dedicated trial with monthly commit and lower unit cost. I'll draft numbers for sales.
omar_se: Enterprise blocker: if they require on-prem PII processing we need Private deploy (~6-8wk). Otherwise Hosted + BYOK + VPC egress is usually fine for pilots.
lucy_sales: Eva  can you share SAML metadata and confirm KMS choice? Proposed demo Wed 9am PST for 90m.
eva_cust: SAML metadata inbound, KMS will be our BYOK plan. Wed 9am PST works, will invite infra.
sec_bot: Note: run appendix A.3 SOC2 artifact check before the demo if they request full docs.
omar_se: Action items: I'll post the Rust sample + test harness today; Ivan publish the one-pager runbook; Taku attach security FAQ and SOC2 excerpt; Sales to confirm calendar and collect SAML metadata.
lucy_sales: Thanks team 4b4 excited to get this moving.
